          "text": "The pattern indexes as **orthorhombic Pnma**, with approximately:\n\n- \\(a=13.9182\\) \u00c5\n- \\(b=4.9212\\) \u00c5\n- \\(c=16.6590\\) \u00c5\n- \\(Z=4\\)\n\nDiagnostic assignments include 002 at 10.61\u00b0, 200 at 12.71\u00b0, 202 at 16.59\u00b0, 011 at 18.79\u00b0, 400 at 25.58\u00b0, 006/015 at 32.22/32.43\u00b0, 404 at 33.54\u00b0, and 020 at 36.49\u00b0.\n\nThe structure is a distorted tetrahalidochromate framework of the Cs\\(_2\\)CuCl\\(_4\\)/\u03b2-K\\(_2\\)SO\\(_4\\) family. The Pnma average structure requires the equatorial Cl/F site to be statistically occupied 1:1. Long-range Cl/F ordering is not supported unambiguously by the powder pattern.\n\n```cif\ndata_Rb2CrI2ClF_Pnma_average\n_audit_creation_method              'Powder XRD indexing and constrained structure solution'\n_chemical_name_common               'dirubidium chromium diiodide chloride fluoride'\n_chemical_formula_structural        'Rb2CrI2ClF'\n_chemical_formula_sum               'Rb2 Cr I2 Cl F'\n_cell_formula_units_Z               4\n\n_cell_length_a                       13.9182\n_cell_length_b                       4.9212\n_cell_length_c                       16.6590\n_cell_angle_alpha                    90\n_cell_angle_beta                     90\n_cell_angle_gamma                    90\n_cell_volume                         1141.0\n\n_space_group_name_H-M_alt           'P n m a'\n_space_group_IT_number              62\n\n_diffrn_radiation_type              'Cu Kalpha1'\n_diffrn_radiation_wavelength        1.5406\n\n_exptl_crystal_density_diffrn       3.09\n\nloop_\n_atom_site_label\n_atom_site_type_symbol\n_atom_site_symmetry_multiplicity\n_atom_site_Wyckoff_symbol\n_atom_site_fract_x\n_atom_site_fract_y\n_atom_site_fract_z\n_atom_site_occupancy\n_atom_site_B_iso_or_equiv\nRb1   Rb   4  c   0.1311   0.2500   0.1030   1.000   1.20\nRb2   Rb   4  c   0.4930   0.2500   0.1640   1.000   1.20\nCr1   Cr   4  c   0.2214   0.2500   0.4170   1.000   0.80\nI1    I    4  c   0.3420   0.2500   0.5750   1.000   1.10\nI2    I    4  c   0.0019   0.2500   0.3792   1.000   1.10\nCl1   Cl   8  d   0.2932   0.0067   0.3572   0.500   1.00\nF1    F    8  d   0.2932   0.0067   0.3572   0.500   1.00\n```\n\nThe principal residual ambiguity is local Cl/F ordering or positional splitting on the 8d site. Such models have essentially the same average powder diffraction pattern and would require anomalous diffraction, neutron diffraction, or local-structure measurements to distinguish.",
